        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- TV Series: The ABC Comedy Hour\n- People: Ronnie Schell, Jack Cassidy\n- Organizations: ABC, Friars Club\n- Works: Hellzapoppin', Gomer Pyle, U.S.M.C.\n- Roles: Duke Slater\n\nFacts:\n- Ronnie Schell was born on December 23, 1931.\n- Ronnie Schell is an American actor, stand-up comedian, and voice actor.\n- Ronnie Schell is probably best known for playing Duke Slater on the 1960s television series Gomer Pyle, U.S.M.C.\n- The ABC Comedy Hour was an American television variety series that aired on ABC in 1972.\n- The remaining six episodes of The ABC Comedy Hour were variety specials.\n- The variety specials on The ABC Comedy Hour included two Friars Club roasts.\n- The variety specials on The ABC Comedy Hour included a revival of the musical Hellzapoppin' starring Jack Cassidy and Ronnie Schell.",
